   113	| `relux-relay-manifest-v1.json` | `scripts/relay_release.py build` writes it inside a full release tree; `verify` and `compare` check it | Retain with the 11-file release-builder tree; pass it to `scripts/relay_asset_smoke.py` | It is build evidence and is **not** copied into the application bundle. Roll back to its retained exact bytes; do not regenerate historical raw Syft metadata and call it equivalent. |
   114	| `relux-relay-assets-v1.json` | `scripts/relay_asset_manifest.py generate` derives it from `relay/asset-bundle-source-v1.json`, the schema, and the retained four-member archive; `check` independently regenerates the expected value in memory | Retain with the accepted source contract and archive; Swift consumes the generated catalog derived from it | This is the only manifest bundled beside the four executables under `relay-assets-v1/`. Rollback regenerates it twice from the known-good contract/archive and requires exact equality. |
   115	
   116	## Rebuild the currently accepted bytes and manifest
   117	
   118	The accepted source and recipe are deliberately split pins. The source commit
   119	predates the final recipe. Therefore a historical rebuild must first verify a
   120	clean source checkout, then overlay only `Makefile`,
   121	`scripts/relay_release.py`, and `relay/toolchain-manifest-v1.json` from the
   122	pinned recipe commit. The combined tree is intentionally not Git-clean, so this
   123	path uses `--require-provenance` through the target builder and separately
   124	proves that compiled source did not change. Do not describe it as a
   125	`--require-clean` build.
   126	
   127	### 1. Obtain the retained known-good archive
   128	
   129	```bash
   130	mkdir -p "$REPO/.temp/relay-known-good"
   131	task-board resource get \
   132	  TASK-260715-24icoz \
   133	  TASK-260715-24icoz_portable-relay-assets.tar.gz \
   134	  --output "$REPO/.temp/relay-known-good/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz"
   135	printf '%s  %s\n' \
   136	  1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e \
   137	  "$REPO/.temp/relay-known-good/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz" \
   138	  | shasum -a 256 --check
   139	```
   140	
   141	Expected result: resource retrieval and `shasum` exit `0`, and the latter
   142	prints `OK`. Any mismatch makes the retained copy suspect; do not extract or
   143	execute it.
   144	
   145	### 2. Make two independent clean source clones
   146	
   147	```bash
   148	SOURCE_COMMIT=58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096
   149	RECIPE_COMMIT=4326036a26a515d5d349e669574323d4d1c7259c
   150	SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1784656987
   151	RELAY_VERSION=0.1.0
   152	REBUILD_ROOT="$(mktemp -d "$REPO/.temp/relay-rebuild.XXXXXX")"
   153	
   154	for RUN_NAME in run-a run-b; do
   155	  RUN="$REBUILD_ROOT/$RUN_NAME"
   156	  git clone --quiet --no-local --no-hardlinks --no-checkout "$REPO" "$RUN"
   157	  git -C "$RUN" checkout --quiet --detach "$SOURCE_COMMIT"
   158	  test -z "$(git -C "$RUN" status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all)"
   159	  git archive "$RECIPE_COMMIT" \
   160	    Makefile scripts/relay_release.py relay/toolchain-manifest-v1.json \
   161	    | tar -x -C "$RUN"
   162	  git -C "$RUN" diff --exit-code "$SOURCE_COMMIT" -- \
   163	    relay/cmd relay/internal relay/go.mod
   164	  python3 "$RUN/scripts/relay_release.py" toolchain-check
   165	done
   166	```
   167	
   168	Expected result: every command exits `0`. The compiled source diff is empty.
   169	Only the declared recipe overlay may differ from the detached source checkout.
   170	
   171	### 3. Build all four targets in both clones
   172	
   173	```bash
   174	for RUN_NAME in run-a run-b; do
   175	  RUN="$REBUILD_ROOT/$RUN_NAME"
   176	  for TARGET_SLUG in darwin-amd64 darwin-arm64 linux-amd64 linux-arm64; do
   177	    TARGET_NAME="${TARGET_SLUG/-//}"
   178	    python3 "$RUN/scripts/relay_release.py" build-target \
   179	      --target "$TARGET_NAME" \
   180	      --go "$PINNED_GO" \
   181	      --go-toolchain local \
   182	      --relay-version "$RELAY_VERSION" \
   183	      --source-commit "$SOURCE_COMMIT" \
   184	      --source-date-epoch "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH" \
   185	      --cache-mode clean \
   186	      --work-dir ".build/relay/work/$TARGET_SLUG" \
   187	      --output ".build/relay/portable/$TARGET_SLUG/relux-relay-$TARGET_SLUG"
   188	  done
   189	done
   190	```
   191	
   192	Successful target builds are intentionally quiet and exit `0`. The builder
   193	verifies the tool provenance, target name, binary format, linkage, Go build
   194	information, version, commit, and target CPU metadata. Any `relay-release:`
   195	diagnostic is red.
   196	
   197	### 4. Normalize, compare, and verify the archive
   198	
   199	The historical byte recipe has no `archive-assets` command. Archive
   200	normalization is non-byte-affecting packaging logic and uses the current safe
   201	writer, which creates an invocation-owned temporary file and atomic final
   202	replacement. The final comparison to the retained archive is authoritative.
   203	
   204	```bash
   205	for RUN_NAME in run-a run-b; do
   206	  RUN="$REBUILD_ROOT/$RUN_NAME"
   207	  cp "$REPO/scripts/relay_release.py" "$RUN/scripts/relay_archive_current.py"
   208	  python3 "$RUN/scripts/relay_archive_current.py" archive-assets \
   209	    --portable-root .build/relay/portable \
   210	    --archive .build/relay/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz \
   211	    --source-date-epoch "$SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH"
   212	done
   213	
   214	cmp "$REBUILD_ROOT/run-a/.build/relay/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz" \
   215	    "$REBUILD_ROOT/run-b/.build/relay/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz"
   216	cmp "$REBUILD_ROOT/run-a/.build/relay/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz" \
   217	    "$REPO/.temp/relay-known-good/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz"
   218	shasum -a 256 "$REBUILD_ROOT/run-a/.build/relay/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz"
   219	```
   220	
   221	Expected result: both `cmp` commands are silent and exit `0`; the archive hash
   222	is exactly `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`.
   223	The four executable hashes must be:
   224	
   225	| File | Bytes | SHA-256 |
   226	| --- | ---: | --- |
   227	| `relux-relay-darwin-amd64` | 2,623,664 | `783b94982e90f0ceed0af0fa11662d11a333e244b87256cbfa0f7d21695f3290` |
   228	| `relux-relay-darwin-arm64` | 2,487,362 | `8ac45b257099c9d2079b0bd2cb9ae489acfb86e443ba7ca7e4b4b2a56380d64c` |
   229	| `relux-relay-linux-amd64` | 2,592,894 | `ddcb22ed4d4a978992a04096abae8adc58d0b8bf3bcdc0c0a006775797e2941f` |
   230	| `relux-relay-linux-arm64` | 2,556,030 | `908b3d9ea3543b6144e2c99407c9aa02cc69e86c1cce80364d32dbdc3de8e0dc` |
   231	
   232	### 5. Regenerate and check the trusted bundle manifest
   233	
   234	```bash
   235	REBUILT_ARCHIVE="$REBUILD_ROOT/run-a/.build/relay/portable-relay-assets.tar.gz"
   236	REBUILT_BUNDLE="$REPO/.build/relay/rebuilt-known-good-bundle"
   237	make relay-asset-bundle-generate \
   238	  RELAY_ASSET_ARCHIVE="$REBUILT_ARCHIVE" \
   239	  RELAY_ASSET_BUNDLE="$REBUILT_BUNDLE"
   240	make relay-asset-bundle-check \
   241	  RELAY_ASSET_ARCHIVE="$REBUILT_ARCHIVE" \
   242	  RELAY_ASSET_BUNDLE="$REBUILT_BUNDLE"
   243	cmp "$REBUILT_BUNDLE/relux-relay-assets-v1.json" \
   244	    "$REPO/.build/relay/relay-assets-v1/relux-relay-assets-v1.json"
   245	```
   246	
   247	Expected tokens are `relay asset manifest generate passed` and
   248	`relay asset manifest check passed`; `cmp` is silent and exits `0`. The bundle
   249	must contain only the four canonical executables and
   250	`relux-relay-assets-v1.json`. This step verifies the archive, schema, ordered
   251	target set, exact bytes, embedded identity, provenance references, generated
   252	Swift lookup, and atomic publication boundary.
   253	
   254	### Historical metadata boundary
   255	
   256	The accepted executable/archive recipe above predates deterministic SPDX
   257	normalization. Raw Syft 1.48.0 output from that historical script contains a
   258	random `documentNamespace` UUID and wall-clock `creationInfo.created`; rebuilding
   259	it changes all four SPDX files and therefore the release-builder manifest and
   260	checksum file. The accepted four executables, normalized archive, and trusted
   261	application manifest are reproducible, but a newly generated historical
   262	11-file release-builder tree is **not** claimed to equal retained historical
   263	metadata. If that old release-builder tree is needed for an audit or rollback,
   264	retrieve and hash its immutable retained bytes. Do not regenerate, normalize
   265	after the fact, or relabel new Syft output as the historical evidence.
   266	
   267	All new candidates must use the deterministic metadata path introduced by
   268	`TASK-260715-1q03sa`: `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` fixes
   269	`creationInfo.created`, the executable name and SHA-256 fix
   270	`documentNamespace`, recursively sorted JSON fixes serialization, and the
   271	comparator checks the exact 11-file release tree plus four protocol-test
   272	executables. The executable audit below proves that supported current path.
   273	
   274	## Strict update procedure
   275	
   276	An update is a new reviewed candidate, not an in-place edit of the accepted
   277	bundle. Execute the following order without bypass. Preserve commands, exit
   278	codes, candidate hashes, and path-free reports in the candidate's task outcome.
   279	
   280	1. **Freeze inputs.** Record candidate `SOURCE_COMMIT`, byte-affecting
   281	   `RECIPE_COMMIT`, `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`, semantic `RELAY_VERSION`, Go/Syft
   282	   identities, target matrix, and approved bundle budget. Keep source and
   283	   recipe commits distinct when they are distinct.
   284	2. **Review source, dependencies, and security.** Review the exact Git diff of
   285	   `relay/cmd`, `relay/internal`, and `relay/go.mod`; confirm `go.sum` remains
   286	   absent and the standard-library-only policy still holds; review Go and Syft
   287	   security advisories and every component/license/source URL change. Update
   288	   authoritative pins, not generated output. A dependency or toolchain change
   289	   is never “checksum only.”
   290	3. **Gate protocol compatibility.** Follow
   291	   `TASK-260715-2z9b4a`, run `make relay-protocol-check`,
   292	   `make relay-protocol-conformance-check`, and
   293	   `make relay-protocol-hostile-diagnostics`. A relay version change does not
   294	   by itself change protocol `1`. A schema, wire value, feature, limit, hello,
   295	   or identity change requires compatible Swift and Go generation plus every
   296	   consumer test; an unsupported protocol bump stops the update.
   297	4. **Review toolchain pins.** Update `relay/toolchain-manifest-v1.json` only
   298	   from immutable official archives and reviewed hashes. Run
   299	   `make relay-toolchain-check relay-toolchain-negative-test` and reprovision
   300	   from retained exact archives. Do not reuse an installed tree after its pin
   301	   changes.
   302	5. **Build in two independent clones.** Use the fresh-clone block below with
   303	   reviewed candidate pins. For a single-commit source/recipe build with no
   304	   overlay, use `--require-clean`. For a split-pin overlay, prove clean source
   305	   first, overlay only the reviewed recipe files, prove the compiled-source
   306	   diff, and use `--require-provenance`; do not falsely add `--require-clean` to
   307	   a deliberately overlaid tree.
   308	6. **Generate notices, deterministic SPDX, and provenance.** In each clone run
   309	   the current `build` action. It must normalize Syft metadata during generation
   310	   and produce exactly four executables, four SPDX documents,
   311	   `relux-relay-manifest-v1.json`, `relux-relay-SHA256SUMS`, the Go notice, and
   312	   four protocol-test executables. Update authoritative source/build provenance
   313	   and dependency inventory, then run `make relay-supply-chain-generate`.
   314	   Notice, inventory, provenance, or deterministic-metadata failure is red. Raw
   315	   historical Syft output is retained evidence, not a reproducibility input.
   316	7. **Prove full reproducibility.** Stage both outputs below one clone's
   317	   `.build/relay/` containment root and run the exact comparator block below.
   318	   Expected output is `relay reproducibility: identical=15/15`; it means 11
   319	   release-builder files plus four protocol-test files matched in mode and
   320	   SHA-256. No semantic exception or unexplained metadata variance is allowed.
   321	   Normalize two four-member archives and require byte-identical archives.
   322	8. **Rotate exact manifest and checksums.** Retain the reviewed candidate
   323	   archive as a task-scoped board outcome. Update
   324	   `relay/asset-bundle-source-v1.json` with its task ID, resource name, archive
   325	   hash, version, source commit, and four exact size/hash tuples. Update
   326	   `relay/supply-chain-source-v1.json` for source, recipe, tool, license, and
   327	   linkage inputs. Regenerate; never hand-edit the compact trusted manifest,
   328	   generated Swift catalog, inventory, provenance, or notices.
   329	9. **Run native smoke on all four targets.** Execute the native block below on
   330	   an unprivileged matching `darwin/amd64`, `darwin/arm64`, `linux/amd64`, and
   331	   `linux/arm64` host. Pass the release-builder
   332	   `relux-relay-manifest-v1.json`, not the trusted-application
   333	   `relux-relay-assets-v1.json`. Each bounded report must have
   334	   `status: "pass"`, matching `target` and `runner.hostTarget`,
   335	   `nativeEvidence.satisfied: true`, and exactly 17 passing checks. Emulation
   336	   and Rosetta are additional evidence only. The four-row workflow is owned by
   337	   `TASK-260715-36gq4m`; do not claim a remote CI row ran locally.
   338	10. **Validate the trusted bundle.** After the reviewed candidate archive and
   339	    `relay/asset-bundle-source-v1.json` have been rotated together, execute the
   340	    two independent generation/check block below and `make
   341	    relay-asset-manifest-test`. Compare both complete five-file bundles. Missing,
   342	    extra, renamed, symlinked, stale, or mismatched content is red.
   343	11. **Validate Apple bundle integration without credentials.** Run
   344	    `make workspace-generate workspace-validate` and
   345	    `make macos-targets-validate`. Confirm the provider contains exactly the
   346	    verified `relay-assets-v1` folder reference. This proves unsigned bundle
   347	    input integration only; it does not prove application signing or
   348	    notarization.
   349	12. **Run downstream bootstrap consumers.** All ten concrete bootstrap tasks
   350	    listed below must pass their selection, upload, remote verification,
   351	    atomic install/reuse, stdio, lifecycle, hostile-output, upgrade, and
   352	    operations tests against the new manifest. They are currently backlog, so
   353	    an update cannot yet claim downstream bootstrap acceptance.
   354	13. **Run M5 release gates.** Execute the M5 validation matrix, product notice
   355	    and SBOM assembly, release provenance, Apple bundle enforcement, signing,
   356	    notarization, attestation, and approval tasks listed below. Only the M5
   357	    release approver can release the containing app.
