## Independent mutation evidence

One copied Linux/amd64 executable mutation changed only the `linux/amd64` manifest entry. Two independent renders produced identical mutated manifest SHA-256 `ba7db4548bd3c974bf6651fc4e9686a4267d2874c74123df6c5af6a09da89579`, distinct from baseline `ef5bd8b3cc41ce0e30c026bd088b370faeea30d789a7c6708631330afe8b049d`; the canonical executable remained unchanged.

Raw relay and protocol-test byte drift, JSON value drift, JSON shape drift, JSON key-order byte drift, file mode drift, symlink substitution, missing entry, extra entry, and FIFO/unsupported entry all rejected. Diagnostics were path-free and included first byte offset and both hashes for byte drift, JSON paths for semantic JSON drift, exact modes for mode drift, and bounded relative names/tree differences for structural drift.

Input gates also rejected a source-commit substitution (exit `1`, `source commit does not match checkout HEAD`) and a Go-tool substitution (exit `1`, `required Go toolchain is go1.26.5`). A third build with epoch `1787158981` completed deterministically but comparison against baseline exited `1` at the changed checksum bytes; its manifest SHA-256 was `7fb715569bf8ecae5282efef4e5c3dc4e2b5af1e55457d78e0df3f958c85feda`.

