+# TASK-260715-u8tkx0 rework results
+
+Date: 2026-08-19
+Role: doc-writer
+Verdict: PASS — ready for independent review
+Scope: build-only relay release/update/audit/rollback documentation; no commit or push
+
+## Result
+
+The runbook now separates the two manifest layers and the two reproducibility claims. The accepted historical lane rebuilds the four exact executables and normalized archive, then independently regenerates the trusted application manifest twice. It explicitly does not claim that historical raw Syft 1.48.0 output is reproducible. New candidates use the accepted deterministic SPDX normalization path and a containment-safe exact 15-file comparator.
+
+The strict update order is source/dependency/security review, protocol compatibility, toolchain review, two independent builds, notices/SPDX/provenance, full reproducibility, four native smoke rows, trusted manifest/checksum rotation, two independent bundle generations/checks, Apple bundle integration, downstream bootstrap consumers, and later M5 release gates. Rollback retains exact known-good bytes/manifests and prohibits execution before verification. Mismatch, unsupported-runtime, notice failure, bundle drift, compromised asset/source/tool response, revocation/rotation ownership, and credential-safe evidence rules remain explicit.
+
+## Fresh operator reproduction
+
+- Prerequisite identity and `make relay-supply-chain-audit`: exit 0; audit token `relay supply-chain audit: pass`.
+- Retained `TASK-260715-24icoz` archive retrieval and SHA-256 check: exit 0.
+- Historical split-pin lane: two no-local/no-hardlink clones, eight clean-cache target builds, compiled-source diff, toolchain checks, archive generation, cross-run comparison, and retained-archive comparison all exit 0.
+- Historical archive SHA-256: `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`. All four documented executable sizes and hashes match.
+- Two independent trusted application bundle generations/checks: exit 0; complete five-file trees and `relux-relay-assets-v1.json` compare exactly with each other and the default accepted bundle.
+- Copied bundle size drift: expected make exit 2 with `relay asset size does not match the manifest`; no suspect executable ran.
+- Deterministic full-release lane: two fresh clones at source `e8bd954a1985e0a3204504209f1b022f71e4d1f9`, recipe `f21e24e25426bfafebb7f47b9f6d00f5c43d3e91`, relay version `0.0.0`, and epoch `1787158980`; both builds exit 0.
+- Containment-safe comparator: exit 0, `relay reproducibility: identical=15/15`; exact tree count is 11 release files plus four protocol-test files.
+- Deterministic archive comparison: exit 0, SHA-256 `09014b22e694b1ff4ab664c81d46b3afccd5a973f701cbd4625bfd88c093ab40`. Release-builder manifest SHA-256: `ef5bd8b3cc41ce0e30c026bd088b370faeea30d789a7c6708631330afe8b049d`.
+- Native Darwin/arm64 smoke: exit 0; bounded report has matching target/host, native evidence true, and 17/17 passing checks.
+- Unsupported native Linux/amd64 request on Darwin/arm64: expected exit 1, `native_runner_identity_mismatch`, no artifact observation, and no process start.
+
+One preliminary deterministic rerun used the draft's incorrect reference relay version `0.1.0`; it still compared 15/15 but correctly produced different archive/manifest hashes. That command exited 0 with archive `68965e793307a3637f1dd97f2e7ee19a9c13a0006755254ab036121f00d1efeb` and manifest `7cb41701db587fca3b913f4d8075b0f593f0cd5cddf93433d05d0d82a6408ff2`. The runbook pin was corrected to the accepted reference value `0.0.0`, and the entire lane was rerun from new clones to the accepted hashes above.
